      "description": "Narenta, anciently Naro, Naron, or Narona, is seated near the Mouth of a River of the same Name, which falling there into the Gulph of Venice, forms a small Bay, called the Bay of Narenta. The City is 50 Miles distant from Spalato to the S.E. and 25 from Ragusa towards the North (Bowen, A Complete system of geography, 36).",
